  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1157 AM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nNorthwest flow sets up Saturday night into Sunday and we will see\nanother weak short wave dig down into Middle TN. This will keep \nshowers and thunderstorms in the forecast through the mid-morning \nhours. Quieter weather sets in by Sunday afternoon as a strong \nupper level ridge to our west slowly builds east some. Highs \nSunday will tick up with most areas seeing lower 90s. Dew points \nwill remain in the low to mid 70s pushing afternoon heat index \nvalues above 100. \n\nThe upper level ridge to our west will influence our weather for \nthe first half of the week and will bring a major warming trend. \nWe will see highs in the 90s with some areas getting close to 100 \non Tuesday. We'll see major heat risk by Tuesday and afternoon \nheat index values will push as hot as 110. A Heat Advisory may be \nneeded for Monday and Tuesday with Tuesday being the hottest day. \nAn upper level trough will push into the Northeast mid-week and \nthat will bring lower heights and cool our temperatures back to \nnear seasonal norms. Overall we will see dry weather throughout \nthe week but could see some low shower and thunderstorm chances \nmid-week as troughing develops over the Northeast.",
